course: dictionary
lesson: 2004
title: Conclusions: the end and the answer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A conclusion is the last part of something, such as the end of a story, an essay or a meeting. Context helps you spot it. «In conclusion, the plant needs light to grow.» The words «In conclusion» tell you this sentence is the ending, where the writer sums up.
explain: A conclusion can also be what you decide is true after thinking about the facts. «She came to a conclusion after looking at all the evidence.» Swap in your meaning: "She decided what was true after thinking" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: People say «jump to conclusions» when they decide an answer before checking. «That is jumping to conclusions: deciding the answer first and checking afterwards, or never.» Good thinkers check the facts first, then decide.
fact: A conclusion is the end or last part of a story, essay or meeting.
fact: A conclusion can be what you decide is true after thinking about the facts.
fact: In science, the conclusion of an experiment says what the results show.
fact: «Draw a conclusion» means decide what is true after thinking about the facts.
fact: «Jump to conclusions» means decide an answer before you have checked it.
exercise: In science, what does the conclusion of an experiment say? | How many people were there | Who won the race | What your favourite colour is | *What the results show
exercise: «That is jumping to conclusions: deciding the answer first and checking afterwards, or never.» What does jumping to conclusions mean? | Running up a hill fast | *Deciding the answer before you check it | Reaching the top of a mountain | Asking a friend for help
exercise: Maya says, «In conclusion, the story ended happily.» Which part of the story is the conclusion? | The first page | The title page | The middle | *The end
test: Which phrase means to decide what is true after thinking about the facts? | Jump to conclusions | Stop and wait | *Draw a conclusion | Run a race
test: «A balanced argument presents points for and against, then gives a conclusion.» What comes last in a balanced argument? | *The conclusion | The points for | The points against | The title
exam: «Agreeing to disagree means accepting that thoughtful people can reach different conclusions.» What does reach different conclusions mean? | Walk in different directions | Forget what they said | *Decide different answers after thinking | Eat different dinners
